  "body": "Ref: https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/custom-elements.html#states-set\n\nThere are many use cases where one needs to target elements using a CSS selector, without touching their DOM. `:state()` would be perfect for this, except it is currently only settable via `ElementInternals`.\n\nCould we consider expanding it to all DOM elements, by adding a `states` property to `Element` (or `HTMLElement`)? Then, `ElementInternals` would just be setting defaults, just like it sets defaults for `role`, ARIA etc. If both sets are non-empty, the resulting state set could be the union of both. Note that this means authors cannot remove a state set via `ElementInternals`, but I think that's okay, and better than the alternative where author states completely supersede internal ones.",
